00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:12.770 align:start position:0%
August 1962 an American u-2 spy plane  flying over communist Cuba takes a  deeply disturbing photograph  imagine you're taking pictures over  hostile country if you saw this alarm  bells would be ringing immediately the  aerial image starts a chain of events  that takes the United States to the  brink of apocalypse the picture was  taken over la Coloma 100 miles from the  Cuban capital Havana it stands out you  can look at this photo and you can see  they're carving this out of very dense  vegetation this seemingly innocuous  image starts a chain reaction that would  bring the u.s. to the brink of war if  you saw these sights on a photograph and  you put them to anybody in the Pentagon  alarm bells will be ringing immediately  the pattern in the image is recognized  as a footprint for a Soviet  anti-aircraft missile system called  an sa-2  if you look at places where the Soviets  help set up sa-2 sites around the world  Cuba Vietnam later in other places they  all have the same looking footprint when  viewed from above looks like a star  David carved into the ground it  it's an unusual pattern but not once you  understand how these sites are  constructed then it starts to make sense  analysts believe the site in the image  was still under construction at the time  the photo was taken  imagery captured three months later by  US spy planes shows a fully operational  missile base the presence of the sa-2  anti-aircraft missiles tips off US  intelligence that the Soviets must be  trying to protect something important  further reconnaissance flights over the  surrounding area soon discover the  Soviet nuclear missiles the US  government could not tolerate deadly  weapons so close to home right next door  in Cuba right across the water the  Russians of the Soviets had a foothold  there was in the mazing ly frightening  prospect  these sites would trigger 13-day crisis  that brought two of the world's biggest  superpowers to the brink of nuclear war  the Strategic Air Command feed 52  bombers  now flying 24-hour mission after intense  negotiations the Russians backed down  and removed their nukes but short-range  tactical missiles remain to protect  Cuban airspace today modern aerial  imagery of the same site shows no trace  of the weaponry that triggered the  crisis the evidence of humanity's brush  with annihilation is gone but not  forgotten
 

